      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a helpful explanation. \n\nI'm actually getting a bit of pushback from one of the directors. They're worried about the \"chaos\" you mentioned—the idea that with so many moving parts and services constantly appearing and disappearing, something is bound to go wrong in the gaps between them. They're asking about \"cascading failures,\" where one small issue in a single service suddenly triggers a massive, unpredictable outage across the whole system.\n\nCould you explain what a cascading failure is in a microservices context and, more importantly, what kind of technical patterns we use to \"contain\" these types of unpredictable, spreading issues to prevent them from taking down the entire infrastructure?",
      "source": "evaluator"
